+/* native hands (this update's native pose) -> camera numbers; with w > 0 move them into the view and IK both arms.
+ * na_mode 1 (default): each native arm is turned rigidly about its own shoulder (and pushed along the arm by D) so the
+ *   native READY hand lands on the guard point G (block: GB; right hand +x, left mirrored). R/D are re-fitted while
+ *   ready/blocking (smoothed, na_tau) and FROZEN while a technique runs (swinging/recovering), so a native punch moves
+ *   the fist exactly as the native arm moves, starting from the guard. Turning the whole arm about the shoulder keeps
+ *   the native elbow and wrist bends (no wrist fold); the push D is taken up by the usual upper-arm stretch.
+ * na_mode 0: rigid turn of both hands about the shoulder midpoint (na_pitch/na_yaw/na_off/na_spread). */
+static int   g_vm_na_mode = 2;   /* POC 2026-10-10 (4080): mode 2 kept the fists nearest the view; mode 1 sent the left hand over the head */
+static Vec3  g_vm_na_g = { 1.3f, -1.2f, 4.4f }, g_vm_na_gb = { 0.9f, -0.3f, 4.2f };   /* R hand; L = mirrored x */
